You need to compute a checksum over 50 million numbers in a request handler without freezing the server. Rewrite this so it yields to the event loop between chunks, keeping it `async`:

```js
function checksum(arr) {
  let h = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + arr[i]) | 0;
  return h;
}
```

Why is `await Promise.resolve()` between chunks **not** enough?

questions.answer:
```js
const yieldToLoop = () => new Promise((r) => setImmediate(r));

async function checksum(arr, chunk = 500_000) {
  let h = 0;
  for (let start = 0; start < arr.length; start += chunk) {
    const end = Math.min(start + chunk, arr.length);
    for (let i = start; i < end; i++) h = (h * 31 + arr[i]) | 0;
    await yieldToLoop();   // macrotask boundary: I/O and timers get a turn
  }
  return h;
}
```
A resolved-promise `await` is a microtask; microtasks all run before the loop moves on, so it never lets I/O in.
